{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains","id":1456700,"title":"Faeify Fairytale Heroes and Villains","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-12T14:27:05-07:00","id":1456700,"title":"Faeify Fairytale Heroes and Villains","content":"What I especially miss from classic <b><i>World of Darkness</i></b> and wish had been included in the <b><i>God Machine Chronicles</i></b> was the interesting characterization and introducing folklore heroes and villains as creatures of darkness. This is especially true for <b><i>Changeling: The Lost </i></b>since changelings are supposed to be fairytales heroes and villains. I know many players think this is unlikely, but I turned in my character of <b><i>Edgar Allen Poe</i></b> as a changeling with the hopes they might include him in a Night Horrors rulebook or even an epic changeling core book that focuses on epic Changelings.<br /> <br /> It is my hope that if enough people turn in ideas for fairytales characters as Changelings; Hansel and Gretel, Little Red Riding Hood, Undine, Alice Liddell, the game designers might introduce them in the Changeling rulebook line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T14:28:40-07:00","id":1456701,"title":"","content":"So if you would turn a fairytale character into a Changeling what seeming and kith would you give them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T15:56:43-07:00","id":1456711,"title":"","content":"This is one I'm sure you'll appreciate.<br /> <br /> Wendy Moira Angela Darling. Fairest.<br /> <br /> Wendy was always a precocious and imaginative child, and often played make believe with her brothers. When the being called the Pan came to her window, seeking his shadow, she was ready for whatever adventure she found. That's how she found Neverland.<br /> <br /> There,she never aged. The world was magical and deadly. It was exciting and wondrous and terrible. She'd gotten diseases she'd only heard of in books, and met monsters she had always hoped were real. The biggest monster of them all, as she found out, was the Pan itself.<br /> <br /> The whimsical creature had decided she would be the mother to his Lost boys, a ragtag band of children he had whisked off for adventure. And she did so well. She played her role as a good wife and mother, which was something she hated the idea of on Earth. She changed, as did her younger brothers. Over time--she was still human enough to have a vague sense of time compared to the Pan-- she realized that something was wrong. Pan wasn't like them. He didn't notice things like injury, or pain. Even after run ins with pirates and natives, he ignored the injuries and deaths. <br /> <br /> That's when she met Hook. Hook was once a lost boy, he said. He adored Pan, loved him even. But Pan forgot him. On an adventure in another realm, he was left behind, abandoned, marooned, humiliated. Worse, he began to age. He had to survive, and so, he became the one thing Pan hated most--a Pirate.<br /> <br /> He made no excuses for stealing Lost Boys and Natives and selling them to other Gentry. Nor did he care that he had taken many changelings from Earth and traded them in for his freedom. Wendy pitied him, but knew he had to be stopped.<br /> <br /> After Hook's defeat, Wendy realized she wanted to go home. Hook was right about Pan. Hook had told her that he was once like them, a human named Peter. But he was so much more than that. He feared she would end up like Peter, and so was she. So she fled with her brothers in tow. Peter had said his goodbyes, and Wendy knew he would forget about her, too.<br /> <br /> Wendy had been a mother and warrior in the Durance. She was the best mother any ragtag group of kids could have. She had to become mother to her two younger brothers--all three had become Changed, and their Seemings were less suited for the proper Society at the time. It was some time before the London Freehold found her, and helped take her burden.<br /> <br /> Now, Wendy (she doesn't like all of the extra names anymore) is a centennial. She is a prestigious member of the Spring Court (For the youth and vigor and joy she learned in Arcadia never left her). She began an orphanage, to help all lost boy and girls. She fell in love, had a child.. and now even had a grandchild, Moira.<br /> <br /> Some say Moira is married to a man named Peter. They have children of their own now. Wendy is still alive, and has a big secret that she has kept hidden for so long. She wasn't even surprised when she saw the hook-scratch on her walls and the empty beds of children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 08-12-2021, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T16:18:37-07:00","id":1456713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1456711#post1456711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one I'm sure you'll appreciate.<br /> <br /> Wendy Moira Angela Darling. Fairest.<br /> <br /> Wendy was always a precocious and imaginative child, and often played make believe with her brothers. When the being called the Pan came to her window, seeking his shadow, she was ready for whatever adventure she found. That's how she found Neverland.<br /> <br /> There,she never aged. The world was magical and deadly. It was exciting and wondrous and terrible. She'd gotten diseases she'd only heard of in books, and met monsters she had always hoped were real. The biggest monster of them all, as she found out, was the Pan itself.<br /> <br /> The whimsical creature had decided she would be the mother to his Lost boys, a ragtag band of children he had whisked off for adventure. And she did so well. She played her role as a good wife and mother, which was something she hated the idea of on Earth. She changed, as did her younger brothers. Over time--she was still human enough to have a vague sense of time compared to the Pan-- she realized that something was wrong. Pan wasn't like them. He didn't notice things like injury, or pain. Even after run ins with pirates and natives, he ignored the injuries and deaths.<br /> <br /> That's when she met Hook. Hook was once a lost boy, he said. He adored Pan, loved him even. But Pan forgot him. On an adventure in another realm, he was left behind, abandoned, marooned, humiliated. Worse, he began to age. He had to survive, and so, he became the one thing Pan hated most--a Pirate.<br /> <br /> He made no excuses for stealing Lost Boys and Natives and selling them to other Gentry. Nor did he care that he had taken many changelings from Earth and traded them in for his freedom. Wendy pitied him, but knew he had to be stopped.<br /> <br /> After Hook's defeat, Wendy realized she wanted to go home. Hook was right about Pan. Hook had told her that he was once like them, a human named Peter. But he was so much more than that. He feared she would end up like Peter, and so was she. So she fled with her brothers in tow. Peter had said his goodbyes, and Wendy knew he would forget about her, too.<br /> <br /> Wendy had been a mother and warrior in the Durance. She was the best mother any ragtag group of kids could have. She had to become mother to her two younger brothers--all three had become Changed, and their Seemings were less suited for the proper Society at the time. It was some time before the London Freehold found her, and helped take her burden.<br /> <br /> Now, Wendy (she doesn't like all of the extra names anymore) is a centennial. She is a prestigious member of the Spring Court (For the youth and vigor and joy she learned in Arcadia never left her). She began an orphanage, to help all lost boy and girls. She fell in love, had a child.. and now even had a grandchild, Moira.<br /> <br /> Some say Moira is married to a man named Peter. They have children of their own now. Wendy is still alive, and has a big secret that she has kept hidden for so long. She wasn't even surprised when she saw the hook-scratch on her walls and the empty beds of children.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love This<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Do you have Wendy's stats? Also, have you listened to our read Brom's <b><i>Child Thief,</i></b> it is a dark retelling of Peter Pan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T16:20:08-07:00","id":1456714,"title":"","content":"Also, it might be interesting to give Wendy or Peter the <b><i>Lost Boy/Girl </i></b>merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T20:02:08-07:00","id":1456730,"title":"","content":"Because Wendy and Alice are from the Victorian era, I thought I would reup my description of <i><b>Alice Liddell </b></i>as a Chatelaine Fairest. <br /> <br /> On Jul 4, 1862, Charles Dodgson (who wrote under the pen name, Lewis Caroll) went on a boat ride with the three Liddell sisters, Edith, Alice, and Lorina. While Reverend Robinson Duckworth rowed the boat, Alice, the middle sister, began telling Dodgson an entertaining story. She told Dodgson and her sisters how she had followed the white rabbit down the rabbit hole, drank a potion that made her smaller than a mouse, than ate a piece of cake that made her bigger than a house, and nearly drowned in her own tears. Deeply amused, Dodgson went home, thinking of the imagination of children. That night, he had strange dreams of Alice being the maid servant of the White Rabbit, growing to the size of a house, and Alice asking the caterpillar for advice. The next night, Dodgson dreamed of the Cheshire cat with his mad half-moon smile, a baby turning into a big, and Alice chasing after the march hare. The fourth night brought the mad tea party, time stuck eternally at 6 o\u2019clock, and Alice escaping through riddles.<br /> <br /> Dodgson found himself being driven mad by these images; of the queen of Hearts lopping off heads, roses painted red with the blood of her victims, of Alice becoming the queen\u2019s chatelain. He first tried to deal with the visions by writing them down. Eventually, this drove Dodgson to a sexual obsession with Alice and asked her father for her hand in marriage. The family responded by cutting all ties with Dodgson. This did not stop the obsession or visions as Dodgson dreamed of Alice escaping through the looking glass only to end up in the land behind the looking glass and the war between the Black and White Queen. Eventually, Dodgson took the pen name, <i>Lewis Caroll</i>, published his visions/dreams under the duology <b><i>Alice\u2019s Adventures in Wonderland/Through the Looking Glass.</i></b> For the Rest of his life, Charles Dodgson would find himself obsessing over his creative angel/muse.<br /> <br /> Twelve years after her fetch revealed what was happening to her in Arcadia, the real Alice escaped the Hedge and found herself back in London. No longer the na\u00efve and innocent young girl who had followed the white rabbit down the hole, into the land of hearts, and bondage under the Queen of Hearts. She was a hardened warrior who had first escaped through the looking glass and fought in the war between the Black Kingdom and White Kingdom, who fought her way to freedom. Although, you would expect her to join the Summer court, she instead went to the Antlered/Spring court and offered her services. Thanks to the fame brought to her through Lewis Caroll,s writing, she rose very quickly through the Spring court, first joining the Satrapy of Pearls and then joining the Eldritch order, The Charmed Circle. As her fetch acted as a muse for Charles Dodgson/Lewis Caroll, Alice tries to inspire artistic creativity in London\u2019s young folk. In present day, she is one of the Antlered Court\u2019s greatest influencers of art and writing in London.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T23:47:14-07:00","id":1456739,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Story Telling Hints: </i></b>Alice Liddell contains a piece of <b><i>The Queen of Hearts</i></b> in her soul, which has positive and negative effects. The positive effects are that hobgoblins often og out of their way to help her, even taking others goblin debt.<br /> <br /> The negative effects, however, is that on the night of the full moon, <b><i>The Queen of Hearts</i></b> takes over her body and mind turning her into a serial killer. I did a changeling murder mystery chronicle in London, where Alice Liddell, under the influence of <b><i>The Queen,</i></b> turned out to be the killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T02:41:44-07:00","id":1456742,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar935_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"935\" data-vbnamecard=\"935\">Cleverest of Things</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11066_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11066\" data-vbnamecard=\"11066\">Madhatter</a> love your versions of Wendy and Alice. The Fairest always were my favorite seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T13:39:32-07:00","id":1456781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1456714#post1456714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it might be interesting to give Wendy or Peter the <b><i>Lost Boy/Girl </i></b>merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, no. Wendy is an old woman now, and Peter, having become a Charlatan, grew up as well. Wendy hid his faerie nature from him. He grew up banal and mundane. She did everything she could to keep him from returning to Neverland and becoming the monster he once was.<br /> <br /> However, her little brother, Michael.. he probably has it. A century later and he still hasn't aged a day. He is forever that little boy, with his teddy bear token and his safety blanket, even if he's become quite the warrior among the Summer Court of London.<br /> <br /> I haven't actually statted them up yet, as my game takes place in the Metropolis (especially Gotham City), but I would love to try it sometime. I had come up with them a long time ago (my user name is a blatant peter pan reference, and my avatar photo is of me playing Pan the Goblin King, from way back in the day) so 2e would be FUN to use to make Wendy. She'd be resilient, lucky, able to talk down the stubbornest and cleverest of things, and I highly doubt she's entirely forgotten how to fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T14:58:01-07:00","id":1456785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1456781#post1456781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically, no. Wendy is an old woman now, and Peter, having become a Charlatan, grew up as well. Wendy hid his faerie nature from him. He grew up banal and mundane. She did everything she could to keep him from returning to Neverland and becoming the monster he once was.<br /> <br /> However, her little brother, Michael.. he probably has it. A century later and he still hasn't aged a day. He is forever that little boy, with his teddy bear token and his safety blanket, even if he's become quite the warrior among the Summer Court of London.<br /> <br /> I haven't actually statted them up yet, as my game takes place in the Metropolis (especially Gotham City), but I would love to try it sometime. I had come up with them a long time ago (my user name is a blatant peter pan reference, and my avatar photo is of me playing Pan the Goblin King, from way back in the day) so 2e would be FUN to use to make Wendy. She'd be resilient, lucky, able to talk down the stubbornest and cleverest of things, and I highly doubt she's entirely forgotten how to fly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That makes sense. There is something I forgot to mention. In my games, beginning at wyrd 7, the Changelings lifespan is greatly extended.<br /> <br /> Wyrd 7 +150 years<br /> Wyrd 8 +300 years<br /> Wyrd 9 +600 years<br /> Wyrd 10, the changeling is immune to aging , disease, and drugs. With the exception of cold iron, their frailties, the changeling can only take damage from supernatural based attacks.<br /> <br /> I did this specially so I could introduce Morgana le Fey as the queen of the Ashen Court, Mordred as the Winter King, Nimue as a member of the Autumn court, and Hansel and Gretel as the incestuous duo that act as witch and witch hunters for Autumn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T17:49:34-07:00","id":1456790,"title":"","content":"<b>Cleverest of Things: </b><i>In changeling, there are ways to become immortsl, but all of them are pretty intense. Certain Entitlements can do it. There are also likely Goblin Fruits you can use, but will then become dependent on (addiction is a strong word to use but it's not inaccurate). I'd imagine there are other factors that can cause it as well.<br /> <br /> I would honestly run the immortality and eternal youth as separate traits, but ones that a given changeling can have both of. One to represent eternal youth (and immunity to time tampering. If mummies can do it, it can work). The other representing immortality itself.</i><br /> <br /> I agree that eternal youth should not be the only way a changeling obtains immortality. In my games, Alice Liddell has the 1.5 version of <i><b>Long of Days,</b></i> which also negates the penalties of aging. As a result, more than a hundred years later she still looks like a young girl in her late teens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T15:06:00-07:00","id":1456832,"title":"","content":"Note: I forgot to mention that Alice containing a shard of the <b><i>Queen of Hearts</i></b> in her soul is a major plot device, because it allows me to portray her as ally and villain. Alice is unaware of her other personality, having no memory when the <b><i>Queen of Hearts</i></b> takes over her mind. Nor does she suspect she might be behind some of the crimes her former Keeper commits.<br /> <br /> . I have done a changeling murder mystery, where the motley was trying to find out who was beheading changelings at the London freehold. Alice first acted as an ally, providing them with information and even using her contacts to help them. However, on the night of the full moon, the <i>Queen of Hearts</i> to over, revealing Alice to be the killer. Alice then played a game of cat and mouse, chasing the motley throughout the London and its hedge. This lasted until dawn, when Alice\u2019s personality reasserted itself. Alice then proceeded to follow the <b><i>White Rabbit</i></b> through the hedge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T15:33:17-07:00","id":1456834,"title":"","content":"Not exactly a changeling, but Kaguya-hime of Japanese fame could\u2019ve been a fetch. Her being found inside a bamboo could be a poetic reference to being made of bamboo, and her turning away of several marriages being her lacking ideas such as love or political necessities. <br /> <br /> We can\u2019t leave out Snedronningen. Having Kai as changeling, Gerda as Fae-Touched, and the Snow Queen as Gentry is almost too perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T17:47:49-07:00","id":1456842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1456834#post1456834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly a changeling, but Kaguya-hime of Japanese fame could\u2019ve been a fetch. Her being found inside a bamboo could be a poetic reference to being made of bamboo, and her turning away of several marriages being her lacking ideas such as love or political necessities.<br /> <br /> We can\u2019t leave out Snedronningen. Having Kai as changeling, Gerda as Fae-Touched, and the Snow Queen as Gentry is almost too perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually LOVE to see a changeling core book, which focused on Asia and had a special section dedicated to Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T17:50:47-07:00","id":1456844,"title":"","content":"I believe that Susanoo, Fujin and Raijin would make frightening True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T19:58:58-07:00","id":1456851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1456834#post1456834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can\u2019t leave out Snedronningen. Having Kai as changeling, Gerda as Fae-Touched, and the Snow Queen as Gentry is almost too perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I envision kai as a silent arrow/winter court darkling with palewraith kith, Gerda as True Friend Beast, who happens to be a member of the Spring Court (Though she definitely started out as fae-touched).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T05:32:43-07:00","id":1456956,"title":"","content":"Not exactly a fairy tale, but I\u2019m pretty sure <i>someone</i> on the net has tried to reimagine characters from Touhou Project as changelings/hobgoblins/Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T16:41:48-07:00","id":1456985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1456834#post1456834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly a changeling, but Kaguya-hime of Japanese fame could\u2019ve been a fetch. Her being found inside a bamboo could be a poetic reference to being made of bamboo, and her turning away of several marriages being her lacking ideas such as love or political necessities.<br /> <br /> We can\u2019t leave out Snedronningen. Having Kai as changeling, Gerda as Fae-Touched, and the Snow Queen as Gentry is almost too perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is there any chance I could convince you develop these characters as changelings? P.S. you mentioned that you were working on characters for a Changeling Night Horrors book. How is that going?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T17:19:54-07:00","id":1456986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1456985#post1456985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Is there any chance I could convince you develop these characters as changelings? P.S. you mentioned that you were working on characters for a Changeling Night Horrors book. How is that going?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could, but I have too many things in real life to do, so\u2026 um, yeah. I probably won\u2019t touch it until I finish the Legacies in Nameless &amp; Accursed (Mage) and Dark Eras (again, Mage). <br /> <br /> Oh, and that ambitious Night Horrors thing? I was thinking of \u2018earthborn\u2019 or \u2018iron-side\u2019 fae, based on real-life fairy tales\u2026 ie. <i>what this very thread itself is covering</i>, so it\u2019s kinda bit redundant at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-16T21:21:17-07:00","id":1457004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1456986#post1456986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could, but I have too many things in real life to do, so\u2026 um, yeah. I probably won\u2019t touch it until I finish the Legacies in Nameless &amp; Accursed (Mage) and Dark Eras (again, Mage).<br /> <br /> Oh, and that ambitious Night Horrors thing? I was thinking of \u2018earthborn\u2019 or \u2018iron-side\u2019 fae, based on real-life fairy tales\u2026 ie. <i>what this very thread itself is covering</i>, so it\u2019s kinda bit redundant at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha! Well, perhaps someone else can design Gerda and Kai as changelings. I have have sent my entry for Edgar Allen Poe as an Ashen King and plan to send in my entry for Alice Liddell as a spring courtier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T18:05:54-07:00","id":1457063,"title":"","content":"I am hoping to see more ideas for major folktale heroes and villains reimagined as changelings. Below is my idea for Mordred as the Winter King in the U.K. I am currently editing his stats, but plan to eventually send as a potential character for a <b><i>Night Horrors </i></b>rule book. I have already turned in Edgar Allen Poe, and hope more people will send in their ideas as well.<br /> <br /> While there are many retellings of the death and aftermath of Arthur and Mordred, here is its true telling. As Mordred lay dying, the King of the Tuatha De Danann, Nuada of the Silverhand, spirited him away to Arcadia, for he believed that Mordred could be the tool with which the Bristish Isles were returned to the Tuatha De Danann and made a part of Arcadia. Mordred was transformed into a terrible creature with the strength of an ogre, yet who flows like shadow around mundane and magical defenses. He was also trained in fighting styles that were ancient by the time the Tuatha De Danann came to Ireland. He was to be the champion who would drag not only Ireland, BUT ALL of the Isles; England, Scotland, and Wales into Arcadia. Yet before he had been a rival for the crown of England, he had been a hunter dedicated to the protection of mortals against the forces of darkness. It was the vows that he had taken as a member of the <i>Order of the Black Knight</i>, that allowed him to break the magical compulsions and controls the Tuatha De Danann had on his mind, and fight his way out of their hollowed hills and back into Britannia.<br /> When Mordred returned, the seasonal courts were in disarray from the death of King Arthur and the fall of Camelot. Hundreds of former subjects of Camelot were being dragged into slavery in Arcadia. Mordred came to the halls of the Silent arrow and declared himself its new King. He knew that neither Spring nor Summer would accept him, for they blamed Mordred for King Arthur\u2019s death and the fall of Camelot. Yet Mordred was determined to do good and protect the people of Britannia, whether Changeling or mortal. He made pacts and alliances with Morgana Le Fey and Nimue, two of the oldests and most powerful members of the Autumn court. For the next hundred years, Autumn and Winter would be the most powerful seasons in Britannia. The Ashen court would use their secrets of the occult and knowledge of the magics and laws of Arcadia and the Hedge to keep the True Fae and their armies at bay. The Silent arrow fought like a wounded and hungry wolf during winter. They launched guerrilla attacks against loyalists, racketeers, and even vampires of the <i>Legion of Green</i> and their <i>Green Knights. </i>Eventually, The Spring court grew brave and hopeful enough to be joy and revelry, while the Summer court rallied and slew many of the terrible beasts of the Hedge, including the <i>Questing Beast, </i>which foretold Arthur\u2019s death. It was the servants of the <i>True Fae\u2019s </i>to feel fear and sorrow. Stability was returned to Britannia and the Seasonal courts.<br /> In this way, Mordred became one of the unsung heroes of the British Isles.<br /> <br /> Thanks to the works of writers like Sir Thomas Malory, Mordred is reviled as a traitor, spoiled brat, and criminal by most changelings and mortals. Despite this, Mordred has spent that last 1,500 years protecting the British Isles from not just the True Fae, but also Vampires, Pure tribe werewolves, evil mages, and ghosts.<br /> Mordred has three frailties that greatly affect his action.<br /> <br /> His first minor frailty compels him to protect the British Isles as long as he lives.<br /> His mien is so monstrous that mortals that gaze upon it suffer lunacy.<br /> Changelings that gaze on his mien suffer disquiet.<br /> To protect against this, Mordred wears the armor of the <i>Order of the Black Knight.</i><br /> <br /> Mordred\u2019s mien is truly a monstrous sight to behold. He is powerfully built and often mistaken for a member of the Beast or Ogre seeming, though he is in fact a Darkling. His skin is jet black/pure obsidian. His pure gold eyes glow like that of a wolf\u2019s, his ears are large, pointed, and doglike, and his mouth is filled with razor sharp fangs. Shadows literally cling to him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T17:31:54-07:00","id":1457161,"title":"","content":"I just turned in my idea for Alice as a Changeling. I agree that if its just me, it probably won't be put in any core book, but I am hoping that other players will send in their idea for fairytales characters as changelings.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Hansel and Gretel as Autumn courtiers in Germany. This incestuous duo serve their court as both witches and witch hunters. Hansel in an Ogre Gristlegrinder, while Gretel is a Darkling Witchtooth.<br /> <br /> Although Robinhood is revered in a heroic figure who stole from the rich and gave to the poor, in reality he was a well born cut throat, who used the common people for his own ends. Meanwhile the Sherriff of Nottingham was a commoner and the world's most libeled police officer who tried to stop Hoods machinations. Robin Hood is a darkling larcenist while The Sherriff is a Beast Hunter Heart.<br /> <br /> Snow White, Duchess of the Icebound heart, is a fairest snowskin who is famous among the silent arrow for her cold blooded politics which have shaped the seasonal courts in Germany.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T16:55:08-07:00","id":1457613,"title":"","content":"I have definitely turned to folklore and mythology when creating True Fae characters. One True Fae character that I created is based on a video game character that was inspired by a mix of the Chinese legend of the White Snake and Japanese mythology.<br /> <br /> I have also used Morgan le Fay as an inspiration for a True Fae, though I primarily used her earlier characterization as one of many fae sisters who is also benevolent and has no familial ties to King Arthur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26495,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","user":"Shinsoryuu","date":". 08-24-2021, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T19:02:25-07:00","id":1457620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1457613#post1457613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have definitely turned to folklore and mythology when creating True Fae characters. One True Fae character that I created is based on a video game character that was inspired by a mix of Chinese legend of the White Snake and Japanese mythology.<br /> <br /> I have also used Morgan le Fay as an inspiration for a True Fae, though I primarily used her earlier characterization as one of many fae sisters who is also benevolent and has no familial ties to King Arthur.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't supposed you could be convinced to write a character profile for Morgana Le Fay as the Autumn Monarch in The Bristish isles? I am planning to turn in my profile for Mordred as the Winter King after some edits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T20:06:09-07:00","id":1457623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1457620#post1457620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't supposed you could be convinced to write a character profile for Morgana Le Fay as the Autumn Monarch in The Bristish isles? I am planning to turn in my profile for Mordred as the Winter King after some edits.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm putting Morgan in a <i>Changeling The Lost </i>chronicle, she'd be a True Fae rather than a changeling. Her realm would obviously be Avalon, and she'd be the sort of True Fae who doesn't go out of her way to abduct changelings. She'd be the sort of True Fae who would be willing to hand out boons, but only after the one seeking her out does her a favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T21:00:18-07:00","id":1457624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1457623#post1457623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I'm putting Morgan in a <i>Changeling The Lost </i>chronicle, she'd be a True Fae rather than a changeling. Her realm would obviously be Avalon, and she'd be the sort of True Fae who doesn't go out of her way to abduct changelings. She'd be the sort of True Fae who would be willing to hand out boons, but only after the one seeking her out does her a favor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you are interested in exploring Arthurian mythos connection to fae lore, then I would recommend The Fairy Faith in Celtic Countries. You can find it on Sacred Texts, right here: <br /> <a href=\"https://www.sacred-texts.com/neu/celt/ffcc/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">The Fairy-Faith in Celtic Countries Index (sacred-texts.com)</a><br /> <br /> The section on Arthurian mythos can be found here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.sacred-texts.com/neu/celt/ffcc/ffcc250.htm\" target=\"_blank\">The Fairy-Faith in Celtic Countries: The Recorded Fairy-Faith: Chapter V. Brythonic Divinities (sacred-texts.com)</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-24T21:23:54-07:00","id":1457625,"title":"","content":"Avalon is something I did actually use in game, but some what of a different take. Essentially, it's the oldest known Western Freehold. I kinda wanted an old changeling the dreaming vibe, mixed with Lord if the Rings to an extent. Here's kinda a summary.<br /> <br /> Avalon, the Fortunate Isle, land of beauty and youth<br /> <br /> Nobody really knows how old Avalon is. According to it's historians, it has existed since prehistoric times. They point to the Journey West, an inexplicable feeling among some changelings that by travelling west, across the waters, that they will find Paradise. Hyperborean, Avalon, Tir na Nog, the Blessed Isle. It was all of these things, more and less. <br /> <br /> Some point to it's fusion of Garlic and Norse roots, and believed it was once a Freehold on the mainland, at a fusion point between the cultures that would later colonize Britain. Indeed, the Avalonians believe themselves to be the Tuatha de Danaan. When life on the mainland became too dangerous, even with their bargains with the Sun and the Moon, they created a colonizing force that first took Britain, and when the Journey West called them, to Ireland.<br /> <br /> Almost all scholars in Avalon agree that it began with the Seelie and Unseelie, day and night, courts. It is said that then, the twin Kings of Avalon, Avallach (whom the freehold is named for) and Annwn ruled in an infinite war, and had control over the mortal tribes they lived amongst. It is said that Viking Invaders, even thousands of years later, recognized the divide of Light and Dark, and many of their changelings found Avalon. Legends of the conflict between &quot;good faeries and bad faeries&quot; still echo to this day.<br /> <br /> The Avalonians are unsure of when the seasonal courts were born, but remember when they adopted the Seasons, in the days of Joseph of Arimathea and the Holy Grail. It is said that Avallach became King of Spring, Annwyn became King of Winter, and a mighty changeling known as the Morrigan became queen of Autumn. The first Queen of Summer is unknown, but many suspect it to have been Nimue, Morgause, Ygraine, or Arthur himself. The legends of this period are sadly broken, and mostly written my human survivors of the &quot;war of Camelot&quot; and a further Journey West.<br /> <br /> As these conflicts pressed on, Avalon tightened up. It witnessed the war between Arthur and Mordred. It witnessed Morgana le Fay evolve from a changeling into one of THEM. It felt the ways of man pressing ever closer, a danger to their freedom. And so, they once again took the Journey West <br /> <br /> Some avalonian scholars believe they left with the Vikings to find Iceland, Greenland, and eventually Vinland. No one is sure. Others say the first American colony of Avalon was Roanoke and Croatan. Sadly during those ages, as well as much of Avalon's history, information is lost. <br /> <br /> Most scholars agree, however, that Avalon was a strong presence in New York by the time of the American Revolution. They had already integrated Norse Elves with (what would some day become the UK)'s ideas of fairies. But as more and more native american changelings warred with them, or we're adopted or colonized by them, Avalon evolved. It adopted elements of Animism, and remembered that the time of elves was over. And so, they prepared for the Journey West.<br /> <br /> They eventually began the Oregon Trail. And you know how many people died of disentery (XD)<br /> <br /> Now perched in the forests of the Pacific Northwest of the United States (and Southwest of Canada), they are looking to their future.<br /> <br /> Through most of history the Journey West took them to undiscovered lands. Now, they are beginning to wonder what is next. Hawaii? Japan? Russia?<br /> <br /> Aavalonian culture is based on everything they've adopted from the Greeks, the Celts, the Anglo-Saxons, the Norse, the native Americans, the Egyptians, the African Americans, the colonizers, the industrial revolution, the Victorian era, the modern hippes and new age movement. Avalon has evolved, but it hasn't forgotten itself. To this day you can still find an elven maiden on a bridge singing a mournful song in old Finnish, or a grumpy mechanic who'll fix your car as long as you don't mind his gobbledegook mishmash of curse words. Byou can find Hollows that were made thousands of years ago and moved, as well as a hollow built yesterday by the crazy entrepreneur that no one believed was possible. It has long since grown too big for a single island to encompass it,and so it has spread in the Forest of the PNW, and changelings still feel the call to &quot;go west&quot;. Already, Japanese, Hawaiian, and Russian changelings are a regular sight in Avalon, as well as envoys from China and Korea.<br /> <br /> Avalon doesn't know it's next move. It was only a few hundred years ago that they realized their &quot;colonize and acculturate and adapt and adopt&quot; mindset became disturbing to the monarchs. They are unsure if the Journey West has ended, or if they must take another step forward. <br /> <br /> Tonight, their culture is like renfaire and comicon crashed together. While most citizens know better than to dress that way in public among humans, an avalonian court function has everything from ancient Greek and gaelic styles, to Victorian and steampunk, and even now cyberpunk. Native American, African, and some hints of cultures further West like Korea, Japan, China, Hawaii, Australia, etc have been slowly making their way into Avalon. The Avalonians adore them, and are beginning to realize that they've survived long enough to hold a place in the world.<br /> <br /> Emissaries from Tokyo have begun to arrive, as some Avalonians keep going west seeking something new. Avalon itself may be solid, but they can't go around the world and expect to find no one there. Theyre faced with the truth. &quot;What IS the West&quot; is a question many are asking. &quot;We don't have the right&quot;. &quot;We deserve to help whoever we can, even if they don't understand us&quot; &quot;who are we to say any of those things?&quot;<br /> <br /> Avalon is in turmoil. It's hard to be that big and powerful without pissing someone off. Avalon has been built on the backs of so many cultures that it cant even excuse itself anymore. How tightly it's caste system (based on seeming and power levels) is is just one of it's many problems. While none of it's founders are known to exist today besides Morgana and Nimue, Avalon is still not sure if it's leaders are the same old changelings that rules before whether literally or metaphorically.<br /> <br /> Is Avalons time up? Can it be fixed? Should they try to journey West again? Do they need the support of ancient immortal changeings? Why does Morgana have such a beef with them? Was Arthur real, can he come back? Are you happy with your place in this supposed &quot;perfect&quot; changeling society? Are you still Lost?<br /> <br /> Edit: I designed this freehold to be kinda.. bad. Ish. On one hand, it's a colonizers. On the other hand, it adopts and loves and accepts what it comes across. I wanted a freehold that is beautiful and powerful like the elves in LotR, but I also wanted to have the players question their values and what they've done to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 08-25-2021, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T11:19:14-07:00","id":1457641,"title":"","content":"This one is more an urban legend than a fairytale, but I have also thought up a True Fae based on Hasshaku-sama. She doesn't deviate too much from the urban legend, appearing as an 8-foot tall woman with long black hair and usually wearing a simple white dress. Unlike the True Fae I based off of Morgan le Fay, this True Fae definitely spirits people away.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Japanese urban legends, I have also used the kunekune and the jinmenken as inspirations for hobgoblins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T13:38:52-07:00","id":1457644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1457641#post1457641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one is more an urban legend than a fairytale, but I have also thought up a True Fae based on Hasshaku-sama. She doesn't deviate too much from the urban legend, appearing as an 8-foot tall woman with long black hair and usually wearing a simple white dress. Unlike the True Fae I based off of Morgan le Fay, this True Fae definitely spirits people away.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Japanese urban legends, I have also used the kunekune and the jinmenken as inspirations for hobgoblins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea, because of my fascination with the cultures and history of Asia. I would LOVE to see a Changeling book that focused on Asia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T17:26:39-07:00","id":1457662,"title":"","content":"I still feel a little down that Japan did not end up being one of the settings in the Changeling core rulebook. I get that there were a lot of changes after the main writer changed, but as someone who finds Japan to be an interesting setting, it still feels like a bummer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T19:50:58-07:00","id":1457671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1456700-faeify-fairytale-heroes-and-villains?p=1457662#post1457662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still feel a little down that Japan did not end up being one of the settings in the Changeling core rulebook. I get that there were a lot of changes after the main writer changed, but as someone who finds Japan to be an interesting setting, it still feels like a bummer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be interested in a Changeling Asian book that explored not only the different myths and legends around Asia, but also the historical connections between the West and Asia. This could explore western colonization of Asia, Mass immigration of Chinese and Japanese during the late 19th century, and also how Asian Americans are one of the largest growing populations in the United States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T20:00:24-07:00","id":1457946,"title":"","content":"Having read, used, and played <b><i>Chronciles of Darkness, Dark Eras 2, </i></b>I really enjoyed the section on<b><i> Arthur\u2019s Britannia </i></b>using <i>Changeling: Tree, Lake, and Stone. </i>Using Arthurian lore\u2019s connection to fae mythos, I had fun exploring the diplomatic tensions between the Seasonal Courts and Camelot. I was also bale to draw on the least well-known myths, such as Morgana Le Fay being an ally of King Athur rather than an enemy and later myths stuck Merlin in a tree to explain his sudden disappearance from earlier myths. This made me realize that I would like a changeling rule book that explored the many variations of Arthurian myth and its connection to fae lore. W.Y. Evans-Wentz\u2019s <b><i>Fairy Faith in Celtic Culture </i></b>has an entire section dedicated to this. I would enjoy meeting Morgana Le Fey as the Ashen Queen in the Brittish Isles and Nimue as one of the Autumn court\u2019s strongest witches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}